"mandelbrot.mst — the float-arithmetic benchmark, in Bench harness format.

 WINARM (P3 D4): `docs/sprints/sprint_p03_detail.md` asks PERF.md's new
 Windows-ARM64 section for DeltaBlue, Richards AND Mandelbrot, but
 `world/bench/` only had the first two in harness format — the Mandelbrot
 workloads that existed (world/35_mandelbrot.mst, 45_mandelzoom.mst,
 46_mandelvm.mst) all render through a Pixmap into a GUI and time
 themselves per FRAME, which is not comparable across machines and cannot
 be checksum-verified. This file adds nothing new to the VM: it drives the
 EXISTING `Mandelbrot>>escapeAtRe:im:` (world/35_mandelbrot.mst — the
 Strongtalk `fast floats` tour method) over a fixed grid and sums the
 escape counts, which makes the body checksum-verifiable the way
 `docs/cog_bench.md`'s protocol requires.

 Why this workload earns its place next to Richards and DeltaBlue: it is
 the only one in the suite that is pure allocation-free Double arithmetic
 in a tight loop — the JIT's float fast path (VUnbox/FArith/FBox, the
 `<primitive: 100..>` ops of world/08_double.mst) rather than sends and
 allocation. A port that got float boxing or the d8-d15 callee-saved
 convention wrong would show up here and nowhere else.

 Grid: 160 x 120 points over re in [-2.0, 1.2), im in [-1.2, 1.2), maxIter
 200 — 19 200 points, most of them cheap, a band of them at the cap. Fixed
 integer-derived coordinates (not accumulated) so the grid is bit-identical
 on every machine and the checksum is a real cross-build oracle."

"The Bench class below is a VERBATIM inline copy of world/bench/Bench.mst,
 for the reason richards.mst records: `macvm run` loads exactly one file
 plus world.list, and Bench.mst is deliberately NOT in world.list — so a
 standalone `macvm run world/bench/mandelbrot.mst --world world` can only
 resolve the driver line's `Bench` if this file binds it itself.
 Re-definition is a clean reopen, so a bench.list concatenation that loads
 Bench.mst first stays correct. If Bench.mst's harness ever changes,
 refresh this copy."

Object subclass: Bench [
    <classVars: Times>

    Bench class >> vmStats [
        <primitive: 111>
        ^nil
    ]

    Bench class >> run: benchClass named: name inner: inner outer: outer [
        | t0 t1 r ms |
        Times := OrderedCollection new.
        "Warmup (discarded): counters trigger, code compiles, heap settles."
        3 timesRepeat: [
            benchClass setUp.
            r := benchClass runOne.
            (benchClass checkResult: r)
                ifFalse: [ self error: 'benchmark warmup produced a wrong result' ] ].
        outer timesRepeat: [
            benchClass setUp.
            t0 := Smalltalk millisecondClock.
            inner timesRepeat: [
                r := benchClass runOne.
                (benchClass checkResult: r)
                    ifFalse: [ self error: 'benchmark produced a wrong result' ] ].
            t1 := Smalltalk millisecondClock.
            Times add: t1 - t0 ].
        ms := self median: Times.
        Transcript show: name; show: ' '; show: inner printString;
            show: ' '; show: ms printString; cr.
        ^ms
    ]

    "Median of a small OrderedCollection of smis (selection into an Array —
     n is tiny, O(n^2) is fine and keeps this free of sort dependencies)."
    Bench class >> median: aCollection [
        | n arr v least ix |
        n := aCollection size.
        arr := Array new: n.
        ix := 1.
        aCollection do: [:each | arr at: ix put: each. ix := ix + 1 ].
        1 to: (n + 1) // 2 do: [:round |
            least := round.
            round to: n do: [:j |
                (arr at: j) < (arr at: least) ifTrue: [ least := j ] ].
            v := arr at: least.
            arr at: least put: (arr at: round).
            arr at: round put: v ].
        ^arr at: (n + 1) // 2
    ]
]

Object subclass: MandelbrotBenchmark [
    <classVars: M>

    MandelbrotBenchmark class >> setUp [
        M := Mandelbrot new maxIter: 200.
        ^self
    ]

    MandelbrotBenchmark class >> runOne [
        | sum step re im |
        sum := 0.
        step := 0.02.
        0 to: 119 do: [ :py |
            im := -1.2 + (py asDouble * step).
            0 to: 159 do: [ :px |
                re := -2.0 + (px asDouble * step).
                sum := sum + (M escapeAtRe: re im: im) ] ].
        ^sum
    ]

    "Canonical escape-count total for the grid above at maxIter 200. A
     benchmark that stops validating measures nothing (Bench.mst's own
     warning), and this number is ALSO the cross-build oracle: it must be
     byte-identical on macOS ARM64 and Windows ARM64, interpreted and
     compiled, or the float path differs between the two."
    MandelbrotBenchmark class >> checkResult: r [
        ^r = 850452
    ]
]

Bench run: MandelbrotBenchmark named: 'Mandelbrot' inner: 1 outer: 10.
